- side.tsx:59 (ally frames);
- panels.tsx:110 (scoreboard .hscore__face) and :192 and :209 (death recap);
- top.tsx:194 (aface banners), :275 (who__face) and :284 (whodot / kill feed);
- status.tsx:217 (target frame);
- optionally dialbar.tsx:136.
The menus keep portrait.png. Then re-shoot the 1080 scoreboard and kill feed.

RIFT laning phase collapses: the first outer Needle falls at a median of 5.4–6.3 min
FIX: As the reviewer proposes:
- VALE's own 'Dawn Seal' until 7:00;
- needle_outer at about 4,000 HP;
- thin-wave protection;
- 'mid' phase from 10:00 or the second fallen structure;
- soak gate: median first structure 9–12 min on role-correct lineups.

BRIDGE ends through sudden death, which drops structure protection, often with the gate chain still standing
FIX: As the reviewer proposes:
- keep `requires` protection in sudden death;
- replace the protection drop with VALE's own 'Gorge Wind' escalation (stacking Wick buffs and structure resist decay), with a ×2 respawn multiplier;
- retune BRIDGE toward a natural 15–18 min;
- apply the same change to rift_quick;
- soak gate: at most 25% of games end in sudden death, and 0 cores fall with their chain standing.

Reconcile modes_economy.md with content.

Item depth: 13 finished items, the same build every game, top tier almost never reached, no anti-heal
FIX: As the reviewer proposes:
- grow to about 30 finished items with VALE-original counters (a 'Stillwater' grievous family, a burst ward, tank penetration);
- a buildPlan that reads the enemy team, and a support path;
- an economy check once G1 lands;
- a build-diversity probe.

Wave note: New item icons are generated by W2 with the HUD-1 icon spec.

Nurrow finishes last in FRAY, and no soak or balance probe exists
FIX: 1. Nurrow payoff, VALE's own: refund cooldown and extend the silence when hitting a sleeping enemy; reorder her combo.
2. A new _harness/probe_sim_bot_soak.ts that seats role-correct, pickLoadout lineups, with:
   - FRAY average placement 3.5–7.5 per fighter;
   - team win-rate bands only at a sample size that supports them;
